tory along with it  simply put it's gorgeous it's crazy how  much detail  is actually in this game there's bags  people and objects everywhere  truly the highlight of this game it was  a clear progression in the environment  starting in the sewer tunnels of the  deep stink moving to the more livable  warrens then even the more extravagant  high street  even though each area per level is  somewhat the same which does have its  drawbacks from a level to level  comparison they are completely different  something i can't get over is the npc's  reaction to the combat  the combat takes place where npcs are  walking so they'll run at the sound of  gunfire but can also get caught up in  the fighting and can be  shot at the fact that whenever i want i  can just kill a group of npcs is quite  the interesting feeling  there isn't some law enforcement that'll  stop you either which kind of fits with  the theme  seeing as everyone at the bottom is  expendable so a few lives lost is no big  deal and it's even further reinforced by  the plethora of npcs that there are even  if all they do they're a stand and don't  talk it still adds to the overall  environment making it feel like what an  arcology would be  a very large but tight tower with  hundreds of thousands of people in one  area all crammed together  it feels alive and that's what a setting  should be for the story i'm going to  refrain from talking about the later  missions as i don't want to spoil the  later content but if you want to jump  into this completely spoiler free  skip to the time on screen to get to the  last section where we talk about  performance and my overall opinion the  story is actually what intrigued me in  the first place  i had to google what an arcology was as  i had never heard about this word before  this game  but after learning that and reading the  brief synopsis at the beginning it was  something that piqued my interest  and arcology is supposed to be a  self-sufficient tower you live  eat sleep and die in here you never need  to leave the building it has all your  basic necessities but also leisure  activities as well  basically take any city from its  population to its buildings and  businesses and cram it into a giant  skyscraper and that's what you get you  see what i mean you never have to leave  the tower that's why this plot is all  the more fascinating what would happen  if the tower you live in 24 7 was  suddenly not under anyone's command and  the leaders originally owning the tower  went bankrupt this affects everyone from  the top to the bottom  speaking to a character we meet later  named poon we discover that even our  paychecks are on standby so there's no  money given out to the workers this can  lead to poverty  and homelessness and when no one has an  answer to the problem riots can start  and seeing as most people are packing  heat in this tower many people could die  in here this alone  is great and the main reason i want to  continue playing during the story you'll  meet a wide variety of creatures all of  whom have their own personalities making  them seem like actual unique characters  not copy pasted versions of each other  sadly in its one criticism i understand  but still feel the need to bring up this  is only for the main campaign  any characters you meet in the main  story are professionally voiced with  unique dialogue separating them from  each other but the side missions don't  have this  all characters dialogue is garbled or  gibberish and either voiced by the same  person with different levels of audio  being raised to make it sound different  or only by a couple people in gt  operative you'll have access to select  gear and you'll be covered by a premium  y corp insurance policy  this is what i meant earlier i want to  criticize this but i feel like this was  due to having a small budget  as paying for professional or even  amateur voice actors is lots of money  especially when making an rpg which can  have hundreds o