ay  with the attempted realism or  tune it down a bit besides this i do  have one change i would like added or at  least considered and that's rotating the  map  unless i miss something you can't rotate  the map at all it's incredibly painful  trying to see where i  am in relation to a quest or object but  can't tell since i can't rotate the  camera this would also benefit players  who are stuck  or lost thanks to the large amount of  twists and turns the map has  the ascent overall is a good game for 26  dollars you get the elements of an rpg  with a captivating plot as well as the  option to explore the arcology's  numerous levels to your heart's content  while there is some bugs and mechanics  that do bother me greatly i think the  positives of this game can outweigh the  negatives especially if you have game  pass  as what do you have to lose we have now  reached the end of the review  do let me know what you think about the  ascent as well as the new series down  below  as i'm always looking for feedback thank  you all for stopping by  if you're new make sure to subscribe for  more reviews like this as well as essays  on your favorite games  i highly recommend my recent upload in  which i explain why fallout 76  is one of my favorite games of 2021 as  always if you're a returning viewer i  thank you for supporting me by coming  back for another video  and with that take care everyone and  [Music]  goodbye  [Music]  you

